{
  "title": "iOS small cleanups: empty catch, double logging, singleton \
@StateObject, getMonday placement",
  "description": "Four small independent iOS cleanups:\n\
\n\
1. Silent error swallowing (fail-fast violation): \
Ramekin/RecipeFormView.swift:367-377 loadAvailableTags() has `catch is \
CancellationError { } catch { }` with BOTH clauses empty — a failed tag fetch \
is invisible. The analogous RecipeListView.loadTags (:315-319) logs the same \
failure. Log it; consider a shared helper for the cancellation-vs-real-error \
split (the pattern is copy-pasted ~12 places with inconsistent bodies).\n\
\n\
2. Double logging in the share extension: \
RamekinShareExtension/ShareViewController.swift logs nearly every event to \
BOTH DebugLogger.shared and an os.Logger (:28-29, :281-289, :302-350); the \
rest of the app uses only DebugLogger. Pick one (e.g. route DebugLogger \
through os.Logger internally).\n\
\n\
3. Ramekin/ShoppingListView.swift:4 wraps a global singleton in @StateObject \
(`@StateObject private var store = ShoppingListStore.shared`), defeating the \
lifecycle @StateObject manages; store access is otherwise ad hoc \
(RecipeCacheStore.shared, CoreDataStack.shared, UniversalLinkStore.shared, \
AppState via @EnvironmentObject). Standardize how views obtain stores.\n\
\n\
4. Ramekin/MealPlanView.swift:261-267 inlines getMonday(from:) week-start math \
(with a force-unwrapped calendar.date at :266) even though \
Shared/MealPlanDateSupport.swift exists for exactly this. Move it there and \
drop the force unwrap. Note: week-start math is deterministic shared logic \
with a web copy (getMonday in MealPlanPage.tsx) — vectors for it are already \
covered by blocked-shared-test-vectors-remaining-areas; this issue is just the \
placement/unwrap fix.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "ios",
  ],
